# Service runtime

## Purpose

Own service initialization, native resources, readiness inputs, and shutdown through Batter.

## Key entrypoints

`src/lib.rs`: `serve` runs protected startup through `batter::service::start`, then registers the assembled HTTP boundary.
[% if jobs_enabled %]
`serve_with_jobs` also registers the Runledger worker from `crates/<<[ package_name ]>>-jobs`; the public API uses it.
[% endif %]
[% if db_enabled %]
`bootstrap_database` uses Batter's finite `Command` owner for setup and pool closure.
[% endif %]
[% if metrics_enabled %]
`src/metrics.rs`: opt-in OTLP/HTTP export of Batter's metrics catalog, selected by `METRICS_OTLP_ENDPOINT`.
[% endif %]

## Edit here for X

Change service budgets, register background components, or add resource cleanup here.
Business behavior belongs in the application crate; HTTP policy belongs in HTTP crates.
The shared startup budget is 30 seconds, including database connection and migrations
when enabled. Request deadlines live in the HTTP-common crate. These policies are
source-owned, not `.jig.toml` or generated environment settings.

## Invariants

Use `Startup::scoped` with `with_unix_signals` and pass it to `batter::service::start`.
Capture the read-only lifecycle status and operation admission before moving the
supervisor; HTTP surfaces receive only admission and a `ReadinessPolicy`. Register the
assembled boundary with `AssembledHttp::register_in`, never a raw router or
`batter::axum::low_level` helper.
The protected scope exposes stage metadata, cleanup reservation, and supported
registration adapters, not full supervisor control. Register cleanup before any
subsequent fallible startup step. Completion is checked: a startup failure, an
unsuccessful shutdown report, or a coordinator failure is an error.
[% if db_enabled %]
Readiness combines lifecycle, the database health monitor registered by the DB crate,
and HTTP application conditions. The monitor probes independently of traffic, so a
database outage turns readiness unready and recovery restores it without a restart.
PostgreSQL startup uses the DB crate's `connect_in` (`pool_in` plus a bounded probe)
and lease-owned migrations under children of the startup operation context.
[% else %]
Readiness combines lifecycle with HTTP application conditions.
[% endif %]
Never move Batter supervision into application state merely to access the runtime.
Use `Command` and `check_command` for finite work, not an empty service supervisor.
Register native runtimes with descendants through supported managed adapters;
joining a wrapper task alone does not prove its descendants stopped.
[% if metrics_enabled %]
Metrics diagnostics are retained beside the service result and never change it or
the exit code. Do not install another global metrics recorder.
[% endif %]
Shutdown phase allowances share Batter's first-stop clock; scheduling delays consume
the budget. Cleanup has an independent allowance and cannot roll back remote effects.
The `jig dev` proxy force-kills after a two-second SIGTERM grace period, which can
preempt this runtime's longer drain and cleanup. Test full graceful shutdown using
the built binary directly; align production process-manager grace with all phases.

